cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LOREON: Long-Read ONT Metagenomic Pipeline"
version: "2.6"
date-released: 2025-01-01
authors:
  - family-names: Mosca
    given-names: Roberto
    affiliation: "University of Perugia, Department of Pharmaceutical Sciences"
repository-code: "https://github.com/iscka/loreon"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - metagenomics
  - "Oxford Nanopore Technologies"
  - "ITS barcoding"
  - fungi
  - bioinformatics
  - "long-read sequencing"
abstract: >
  LOREON (Long-Read ONT Metagenomic Pipeline) is a comprehensive
  bioinformatics pipeline for processing Oxford Nanopore Technologies (ONT)
  long-read metagenomic sequencing data, specifically designed for fungal
  ITS barcode analysis. It integrates minimap2 alignment, samtools filtering,
  DuckDB-based OTU aggregation, and an interactive HTML report generator
  into a single PyQt5 graphical interface.
